  "family": "Myrtaceae",
  "memo": "&lt;em&gt;Eucalyptus globulus&lt;/em&gt;, commonly known as blue gum, is one of the most widely recognized and extensively planted eucalyptus species. Native to Australia, it has become naturalized in many regions worldwide, particularly in California and Hawaii, where it thrives in Mediterranean climates with mild seasonal variation. In its natural range, &lt;em&gt;E. globulus&lt;/em&gt; often forms dense, pure stands that exclude most understory vegetation. It reproduces both by seed and vegetative sprouting, contributing to its ability to dominate a variety of plant communities. Its rapid growth, high water use, and prolific seed production make it an exceptionally strong competitor, often outcompeting native species and altering local ecosystems.",
